# Commit messages (HW3)

When the user wants a commit message or is about to commit changes under `homework-3/`:

1. Read and follow the **commit-messages** skill at `homework-3/.cursor/skills/commit-messages/SKILL.md`.
2. Run `git status`, `git diff --cached`, and `git log -10 --format="%s"` before drafting.
3. Analyze the **full** diff (spec/docs vs `platform/` code — use scope `docs(homework-3)` or `feat(platform)` when clear).
4. Default output: **recommended** only in a `text` fence. Add **one-liner** or **split-suggestion** only when requested.

**N.B.** Do not commit unless the user explicitly asks.
